{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/643782-the-primordial-dream","id":643782,"title":"The Primordial Dream?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-28T22:38:36-07:00","id":643782,"title":"The Primordial Dream?","content":"So, I need some help in visualizing the realm of the Primordial Dream. What is outside of a chamber? How big can a chamber be? <br /> <br /> Let's break this down into an example. A beast takes an old building in the suburbs and adds it to his lair. While he is in that chamber in the liar, what happens if he walks out the front door? I am pretty sure it is unlike the shadow in that he will see a reflection or version of the physical world, so what is it that he sees? <br /> <br /> Something that further confused me was the hive system. Hives are a &quot;region&quot; of chambers that can include multiple lairs. How can there be a region of chambers, if a beast can have one chamber that he grabbed in America, and then another one in Africa? The book uses an example of an apex of a hive being a werewolf. How can a werewolf, operating in the physical and the shadow, affect a system of chambers in which they might not be anywhere near the werewolf? Does he only need to be near a single chamber to affect a whole hive? And how are chambers in the Primordial Dream &quot;close&quot; to each-other? Is it random? Are the physical chambers supposed to be close to each other? <br /> <br /> Also, as if your explanation to the above wasn't big enough already, I've got another question. What is the size limit of a chamber? A building or a cave system have obvious confines, but what of a forest, or an open plain/desert? Is the Primordial chamber of said forest boxed in by something, lead to a drop-off of nothingness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:52:44-07:00","id":643799,"title":"","content":"To answer in reverse:<br /> <br /> A Chamber is a big as you want it to be. Space in the Primordial Dream is conceptual rather than quantitative. When you're lost in the woods, the forest feels infinite. A Chamber might be a single room in a haunted mansion, or it might be the vast inky depths of the Abyssal Zone. The important part is making sure intruders feel scared upon entry.<br /> <br /> The effects of Hive and Apex seem to be based primarily on the physical location of a monster in question. A Beast who makes his home in Jakarta, even if he has a Chamber connected to Cardiff, is going to see his Lair affected by the monsters of Jakarta. Though I imagine in this case the Cardiff Hive might start making inroads as well. I think it's best to imagine the Apex as whatever the mere mortals in a given area are going to have nightmares about, which affects the local Primordial Dream--the term &quot;local&quot; here referring to the collection of proximity minds all contributing to the same set of ideas and symbols. The &quot;closeness&quot; of Chambers seems to be based on a combination of waking-world proximity and conceptual connections (not to mention Kinship). Maybe the river full of water moccasins in your Lair is connected to the raging whitewater rapids in the Lair of another Beast with whom you have had extended contact.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell the book doesn't go into what the Primordial Dream is like outside of Lairs. I imagine in your example, when the Beast steps outside the front door in the Primordial Dream, either they enter a different Chamber of their Lair, or they continue on within the same chamber according to the dictates of dream logic (as any given Chamber is not a fixed space), or maybe they enter a pathway into another Lair connected to the Hive, or maybe in some extreme case they enter the greater Astral Realm. Or maybe the door doesn't open at all. That's kind of scary, not being able to get out of an old building you stumbled into.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps answer your questions. It's not out of the realm of possibility that I've misinterpreted what you were asking, but all the same, I hope it provides some sort of elucidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:58:22-07:00","id":643801,"title":"","content":"The front door leads to a Burrow or some more abstracted portion of the Beast's mental landscape.<br /> <br /> Beasts being able to open Pathways from one end of the world to the other doesn't make New York City not New York City and if a werewolf is the scariest magical fucker in the collective unconscious of New York City then she's the Apex of New York City. Chambers are made of places that actually exist.<br /> <br /> The setpiece of &quot;a location&quot; is pretty much the delineating factor for a Chamber. The forest stretches as far as is actually considered &quot;the forest,&quot; unless the Chamber's seed is built on some more distinct place within the forest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:22:25-07:00","id":643826,"title":"","content":"Actually your responses did a lot to enlighten me, so thank you. <br /> <br /> I suppose it was because I was stuck on an objective answer of &quot;this is what is out there&quot; as opposed to &quot;It's whatever the hell you want&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7474-tylerjohnny1","name":"Tylerjohnny1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7474_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T04:15:11-07:00","id":643927,"title":"","content":"I recommend getting your hands on the Astral Realms book if you can. Honestly, a lot of your questions are easily answerable once you get a good understanding of the realm. The Beast book doesn't describe it in the detail necessary for really exploring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T02:48:30-07:00","id":647805,"title":"","content":"Spot on with the Chamber descriptions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only other thing that I might add to this is that a Hive draws resident Chambers within the &quot;region&quot; of the Hive closer to the waking world. Places that serve as doors to the Primordial Dream not only open more regularly but the mortal and supernatural citizens become more aware that something is off or wrong about these Chambers. On some level everybody in a Hive realizes that they live in a domain of nightmares, it's just easier for mortals and other supernaturals to suppress these feeling because they already have enough immediate problems to deal with on a regular basis. In a game mechanic sense this is why the Apex influences the Chambers of a Hive. It doesn't just show that the Apex is powerful enough to influence the Primordial Dream just with it's presence, but that it's also able to influence the World of Darkness itself by having it's Legend spread so thoughouly that any place in a Hive slightly associated with the Apex could potentially open up into any Beat's Lair.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's take the Werewolf Apex. Let's say for the sake of example that it's a mean ass Hunter in Darkness who stalks prey who violate it's territory through the many backallies of...let's say New York City. Word begins to spread about the Stalker and how you should never go down dark allyways after dark (Mechanically giving all Lairs the Darkness Trait.) Because it's common knowledge to expect danger and death to come from the dark places of the city the Primordial Dream make it so that any place with the Darkness Tilt could become a Primordial Pathway to any Beast's Lair if they make the Hive their home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:40:27-07:00","id":647893,"title":"","content":"The location the chambers are assimilated from doesn't really matter. All that counts is they are sympathetic to what your lair represents. You could have a chamber from America, Ireland, Japan and Russia as long as they all share a similar theme to each other. It's also been speculated if not flat out stated that a Beast can enter or exit their lair from any place that shares a sympathetic connection. For example, a Makara who's lair resembles a large body of water could enter their lair through any water deep enough to swim in, as well as exit their lair through any such point. In other words, Beasts have the power to perform long distance travel thanks to their lairs! Assuming that they know the location exists ahead of time, I would imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what happens if you walk through the front door; how often have you had a dream where the scenery changes in the blink of an eye and you don't notice until later? It's not difficult to imagine that leaving through that door would take you to another chamber by dropping you in the middle of a decaying tree fort or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-01-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}